      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "widget_ue_connectable": {}
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "I generally just use \"Upscale Image\" as it is fast and simple.\n\nI mix GIMM and RIFE for interpolation just because.\n\nInbound video is 16fps, GIMM takes it to 32 fps, RIFE takes that to 64fps. \n\nI aim for 1920 x 1080 and 64fps which is final cut for Davinci Resolve (actually 60fps in the free version)\n\n\n---\n\nthe other upscalers have their place, but will add 15 mins compared to the Upscale Image which is the baseline version.\n\nrealESRGAN x2 (original model) - its very good and super crisp on blurry stuff but maybe too crisp on only slightly blurry.\n\n1x NMDKh264texture - tries to add texture back in to compressed video blur, not tested much but hasnt yet been better than ESRGAN x2.\n\n1xSkinContrast-High-SuperUltraCompact - for skin trying to remove plastic look but wasnt overly impressed.\n\n(Beware of x4 taking 1 hour with video, check the command prompt when running)\n\nsee more on the site https://openmodeldb.info/?t=video-frame\n\nbest upscalers are probably NMKD and try more from his site - https://icedrive.net/s/43GNBihZyi\n\n---\n\nto upscale 1024 x 576 to 1920 x 1080 multiply by roughly 1.9\n\nto upscale 832 x 480 to 1920 x 1080 multiply by roughly 2.3 (its a little under)\n\n"
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
